# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Some pre-existing article bodies link to individual articles using the
# plural listing prefix (/articles/<YYYY-MM>/<slug>) instead of the correct
# singular article route (/article/<YYYY-MM>/<slug>). The plural prefix is
# also used, on its own, by the real paginated article-listing route
# (/articles/2, /articles/3, ...), which has only ONE path segment after
# /articles/. This rule requires exactly TWO segments (:year/:slug), so it
# cannot match the single-segment pagination URLs and leaves them untouched.
/articles/:year/:slug  /article/:year/:slug  301
